&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
margin-left:0cm;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-fareast-language:
EN-GB&quot;&gt;The proposed quantum massing of development would be unacceptable within
the existing plot of land due to the potential impact to the immediately
adjacent to the Greenway Avenue Wood SINC given that there has not been a
sufficient habitats regulation assessment provided, and thus the development is
not in accordance with Policy 79 of the&amp;nbsp;Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1
(2024).&amp;nbsp;In addition to this, insufficient information has been submitted
with regards to the hard landscaping and boundary treatments on site for the
LPA to make an assessment on their suitability to the scheme, which is in
contrary to Policy 53 of Waltham Forests Local Development Plan LP1 (2024). &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
margin-left:0cm;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-fareast-language:
EN-GB&quot;&gt;Insufficient detail has been provided with regards to the hard and soft
landscaping for the development, as such officers are unable to determine any harm
caused to the nearby species, habitats and wildlife or the visual amenities of
the surrounding vicinity, which is contrary to Policy 53 and 79 of Waltham
Forests Local Development Plan LP1 (2024). &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
margin-left:0cm;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-fareast-language:
EN-GB&quot;&gt;Insufficient information has been submitted to allows officers to assess
whether the proposed development would appropriately mitigate and offset any
surface water to ensure there is no harmful impact to the adjacent sites, in
contrary to Policy 91 of Waltham Forests Local Development Plan LP1 (2024) and
Policy S1 of the London Plan (2021).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:18.0pt;margin-right:-34.6pt;margin-bottom:
12.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;
mso-fareast-language:EN-GB&quot;&gt;By way of the submitted Ecological Impact Appraisal
which is outdated, insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate
that the proposed development would not have a significant biodiversity or
geodiversity impact on the adjacent Site of Special Scientific interest, or the
Greenway Avenue Wood and the Epping Forest North SINCs. Officers are therefore
unable to assess the impact of the development on these designated
environmental sites. The proposed development is therefore contrary to Policy
G6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy 79 of the London Borough Waltham Forest
Local Plan Part One (2024).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:18.0pt;margin-right:-34.6pt;margin-bottom:
12.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;
mso-fareast-language:EN-GB&quot;&gt;By way of the submitted Arboriculture and Method
Statement report which is outdated, insufficient information has been submitted
to allow officers to assess whether the proposed development would cause harm
to the trees onsite and adjacent to the site during demolition works,
construction and post-construction. As such, in the absence of this
information, the application fails to comply with Policy 80 of Waltham Forests
Local Development Plan LP1 (2024), Policy G7 of the London Plan (2021).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
margin-left:0cm;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-fareast-language:
EN-GB&quot;&gt;The proposal fails to demonstrate how the development would achieve the highest
standards of fire safety in regard to its design in incorporating appropriate features
which reduce the risk to life in the event of a fire, its construction methods,
means of escape, strategy of evacuation and providing suitable access and equipment
for firefighting appropriate for the size and use of the development. This is contrary
to Policy 6 of the Waltham Forest Local Development Plan (2024) and Policy D12
of the London Plan (2021). &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB&quot;&gt;5 Notwithstanding
the first reason for refusal, the applicant has failed to enter into a S106
agreement and therefore is not in compliance with Policies 60, 61, 62, 81 and
94 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024), Policies T1, T2, T3 and
T4 of the London Plan (2021) and Supplementary Planning Document – Planning
Obligations (2017), specifically in relation to the following planning
obligation requirements:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;













